i {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal/country"} "Medals by country"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal/athlete"} "Medals by athlete"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal_table"} "Medal tables"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/participation"} "Participations"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/records"} "Olympic Records"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/age"} "Age records"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/age_at_death"} "Age at death"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/lists"} "Lists"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/today"} "Today"]] "\n" [:li {}] "\n" [:li {:class "divider"}] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics"} "Statistics"]] "\n"] "\n"] "\n\n\n\n\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/feedbacks/new"} "Feedback"]] "\n" [:form {:class "navbar-form navbar-left", :role "search", :action "/athletes/quick_search", :accept-charset "UTF-8", :method "post"} [:input {:name "utf8", :type "hidden", :value "✓", :autocomplete "off"}] [:input {:type "hidden", :name "authenticity_token", :value "bd5z0uvZBbdkhRa4bhvyzzfN22NlCxEbTCvnP339j65SlBzDSXVq8BXRWcw2U7g1S1-jwCWT4JHXrfDsUyc4Gw", :autocomplete "off"}] [:div {:class "form-group"} "\n" [:input {:type "text", :name "query", :id "query", :class "form-control", :placeholder "Athlete search"}] "\n"] "\n" [:input {:type "submit", :name "commit", :value "Go", :class "btn btn-default", :data-disable-with "Go"}] "\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "container"} "\n" [:ol {:class "breadcrumb"} "\n" [:li {} "\n" [:a {:href "/"} "Home"] "\n"] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/editions"} "Games"]] [:li {:class "active"} "1948 Winter Olympics Overview"] "\n"] "\n\n\n" [:h1 {} "1948 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:h2 {} "Facts"] "\n" [:table {:class "biotable"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Competition type"] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic Games"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Number and Year"] "\n" [:td {} "V / 1948"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Host city"] "\n" [:td {} "\nSankt Moritz, Switzerland\n(" [:a {:href "/venues/editions/33"} "Venues"] ")\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Opening ceremony"] "\n" [:td {} "\n30 January\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Closing ceremony"] "\n" [:td {} "\n 8 February\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Competition dates"] "\n" [:td {} "\n30 January –  8 February\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:td {} "\n" [:a {:href "/counts/edition/33"} "667"] "\nfrom " [:a {:href "/editions/33/countries"} "28 countries"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal events"] "\n" [:td {} "\n22\nin 9 disciplines\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Other events"] "\n" [:td {} "\n2\nin 2 disciplines\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "\nOverview\n\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The world returned to Winter Olympia after an enforced absence of 12 years.  St. Moritz was chosen because all of the sites that they had used in " [:a {:href "/editions/30"} "1928"] " were still available, and the Swiss resort could organize the Games much quicker than any other city, with the possible exception of " [:a {:href "/editions/32"} "Germany’s 1936 site"] ", Garmisch-Partenkirchen, which was not even considered.  In fact, Germany and its Axis partner, Japan, were not invited to the Olympic Games in 1948 in either St. Moritz or " [:a {:href "/editions/12"} "London"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Another small political protest occurred when Lebanon, the only Arab state entered, protested the entry of a Palestine team, which actually represented the nascent Jewish state, was composed of an all-Jewish team, and planned on carrying a Zionist flag.  Fortunately, the Palestine team withdrew because the team did not have adequate time to prepare."] "\n\n" [:p {} "St. Moritz hurriedly put together excellent arrangements for the Games that were again disturbed, though less severely, by the “Föhn” wind.  This time, " [:a {:href "/results/20123"} "ice hockey"] " matches (held outdoors) and the " [:a {:href "/results/996"} "10,000 metres speed skating"] " had to be delayed, but no events were cancelled this time, as they had been in 1928."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/editions/33/sports/ALP"} "Alpine skiing"] " made its true Olympic début.  A combined event had been held in " [:a {:href ""} "1936"] " but, this time, there were three events for both men and women.  Two athletes won a second “St. Moritz” Olympic medal: " [:a {:href "/athletes/98337"} "“Bibi” Torriani"] " played on the Swiss ice hockey team to match his bronze from " [:a {:href "/results/20038"} "1928"] "; and " [:a {:href "/athletes/86531"} "Jack Heaton"] " (USA) also repeated his silver medal from the " [:a {:href "/results/1"} "skeleton race in 1928"] ", on the famed " [:a {:href "/venues/149"} "Cresta Run"] ".  The skeleton race, a form of tobogganing unique to the St. Moritz resort, was " [:a {:href "/results/6"} "held at the Olympics for only the second time"] ", and some thought, last time.  However, skeleton was restored to the Olympic Programme and returned to the Olympics in " [:a {:href "/editions/47/sports/SKN"} "2002 at Salt Lake City"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The major dispute of the 1948 Winter Olympics occurred in ice hockey.  The Americans sent over two teams, one representing the U.S. Olympic Committee (USOC) and one representing the American Hockey Association of the United States (AHAUS).  The AHAUS team was affiliated with the " [:a {:href "/organizations/130"} "International Ice Hockey Federation"] " (IIHF) but not the USOC.  The IIHF accepted the AHAUS entry over the protests of the " [:a {:href "/organizations/1"} "IOC"] ".  USOC President " [:a {:href "/athletes/78168"} "Avery Brundage"] " declared that, if the AHAUS team was approved, the entire United States’ team would withdraw.  The IOC then ruled that neither team could compete, but was overruled by the Swiss Organizing Committee, which accepted the AHAUS entry.  The AHAUS team played in the tournament and finished fourth, but was then disqualified by the IOC and their finish declared void.  The other United States’ athletes did not withdraw, as Brundage had promised.  Amazingly, even though only the AHAUS players competed in the Olympic contests, the USOC today does not carry their names on their database of Olympians, but does carry the names of the USOC team that did not play one minute in the Olympics."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Bid process"] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "St. Moritz (Switzerland) was proposed as the host for the 1948 Olympic Winter Games in the postal vote which was mailed for selection of the 1948 Olympic Games host city. St. Moritz was confirmed by acclamation at the 40th " [:a {:href "/meetings"} "IOC Session"] " in Lausanne, on 6 September 1946. Lake Placid, New York (United States) had also shown interest in hosting these Games."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Ceremonies"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped table-condensed"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} [:a {:href "/ceremonies/officially_opened"} "Officially opened by"]] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/1100030"} "Enrico Celio"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {}] [:td {} "President"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} [:a {:href "/ceremonies/athlete_oath"} "Taker of the Athlete's Oath"]] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/98337"} "Bibi Torriani"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} "Ice Hockey"] [:td {}] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} [:a {:href "/ceremonies"} "Flagbearers"]] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/flagbearers?edition_id=33"} "Full list"]] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Medal Disciplines"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} "\n" [:a {:href "/editions/33/sports/ALP"} "Al